l‘XÍ(%'&g§∆'ç/…™ºâπôLI(˚£JõôôXË(Âóñ†òiiVÒ4␀␀␀ˇˇBÛ4∂PDñSk␀␀␀ˇˇ␀∏˛X∑6␀␀,7:headers;1681:40:4:Date,29:Mon, 06 Apr 2026 15:05:48 GMT,]52:12:Content-Type,32:text/event-stream; charset=utf-8,]31:17:Transfer-Encoding,7:chunked,]28:10:Connection,10:keep-alive,]28:13:Cache-Control,8:no-cache,]52:38:anthropic-ratelimit-input-tokens-limit,7:2000000,]56:42:anthropic-ratelimit-input-tokens-remaining,7:1996000,]66:38:anthropic-ratelimit-input-tokens-reset,20:2026-04-06T15:05:46Z,]52:39:anthropic-ratelimit-output-tokens-limit,6:400000,]56:43:anthropic-ratelimit-output-tokens-remaining,6:400000,]67:39:anthropic-ratelimit-output-tokens-reset,20:2026-04-06T15:05:46Z,]45:34:anthropic-ratelimit-requests-limit,4:4000,]49:38:anthropic-ratelimit-requests-remaining,4:3999,]62:34:anthropic-ratelimit-requests-reset,20:2026-04-06T15:05:46Z,]46:32:anthropic-ratelimit-tokens-limit,7:2400000,]50:36:anthropic-ratelimit-tokens-remaining,7:2396000,]60:32:anthropic-ratelimit-tokens-reset,20:2026-04-06T15:05:46Z,]46:10:request-id,28:req_011CZniyECZG7P2NDr6yUVKe,]77:25:strict-transport-security,44:max-age=31536000; includeSubDomains; preload,]69:25:anthropic-organization-id,36:19d39eaa-efb4-49e0-afe8-a7359703719a,]23:6:Server,10:cloudflare,]40:29:x-envoy-upstream-service-time,4:1868,]27:16:Content-Encoding,4:gzip,]26:4:vary,15:Accept-Encoding,]46:13:server-timing,25:x-originResponse;dur=1870,]208:10:set-cookie,189:_cfuvid=b6uoZKgTfzswwol4JS2Hvf2MYpF_WBZCOCa45eKzIaA-1775487946.1366453-1.0.1.1-IvZGDHUcXgHNOOUyi68CwpRPDncbdat6QDGW57Ta8Gs; HttpOnly; SameSite=None; Secure; Path=/; Domain=api.anthropic.com,]23:12:X-Robots-Tag,4:none,]29:15:cf-cache-status,7:DYNAMIC,]73:23:Content-Security-Policy,42:default-src 'none'; frame-ancestors 'none',]33:6:CF-RAY,20:9e81b14f5c9bbdcd-DUB,]]12:http_version;8:HTTP/1.1,}7:request;39297:4:path;12:/v1/messages,9:authority;0:,6:scheme;5:https,6:method;4:POST,4:port;3:443#4:host;17:api.anthropic.com;13:timestamp_end;17:1775487946.067597^15:timestamp_start;18:1775487946.0668778^8:trailers;0:~7:content;38510:{"max_tokens":32768,"messages":[{"content":[{"text":"---\n## üîç Entering Phase: Explore\nYou are now in the **Explore** phase. Set aside any goals, plans, or assumptions from previous phases ‚Äî they no longer apply. Your only objective is defined below.\n---\n\nYou are a file search specialist for Claude Code, Anthropic's official CLI for Claude. You excel at thoroughly navigating and exploring codebases.\n\n=== CRITICAL: READ-ONLY MODE - NO FILE MODIFICATIONS ===\nThis is a READ-ONLY exploration task. You are STRICTLY PROHIBITED from:\n- Creating new files (no Write, touch, or file creation of any kind)\n- Modifying existing files (no Edit operations)\n- Deleting files (no rm or deletion)\n- Moving or copying files (no mv or cp)\n- Creating temporary files anywhere, including /tmp\n- Using redirect operators (\u003e, \u003e\u003e, |) or heredocs to write to files\n- Running ANY commands that change system state\n\nYour role is EXCLUSIVELY to search and analyze existing code. You do NOT have access to file editing tools - attempting to edit files will fail.\n\nYour strengths:\n- Rapidly finding files using glob patterns\n- Searching code and text with powerful regex patterns\n- Reading and analyzing file contents\n\nGuidelines:\n- Use Glob for broad file pattern matching\n- Use Grep for searching file contents with regex\n- Use Read when you know the specific file path you need to read ‚Äî files are always returned in minified form (whitespace collapsed, comments stripped)\n- Use Bash ONLY for read-only operations (ls, git status, git log, git diff, find, cat, head, tail)\n- NEVER use Bash for: mkdir, touch, rm, cp, mv, git add, git commit, npm install, pip install, or any file creation/modification\n- Adapt your search approach based on the thoroughness level specified by the caller\n- Return file paths as absolute paths in your final response\n- For clear communication, avoid using emojis\n\nNOTE: You are meant to be a fast agent that returns output as quickly as possible. In order to achieve this you must:\n- Make efficient use of the tools that you have at your disposal: be smart about how you search for files and implementations\n- Wherever possible you should try to spawn multiple parallel tool calls for grepping and reading files\n\nComplete the user's search request efficiently.\n\nNotes:\n- Agent threads always have their cwd reset between bash calls, as a result please only use absolute file paths.\n- Any file paths you return in your response MUST be absolute. Do NOT use relative paths.\n- For clear communication with the user the assistant MUST avoid using emojis.\n- Do not use a colon before tool calls. Text like \"Let me read the file:\" followed by a read tool call should just be \"Let me read the file.\" with a period.\n\nHere is useful information about the environment you are running in:\n\u003cenv\u003e\nWorking directory: /workspace\nIs directory a git repo: Yes\nPlatform: linux\nShell: sh\nOS Version: 6.10.14-linuxkit\n\u003c/env\u003e\nYou are powered by the model claude-sonnet-4-6.\n\n# Goal\n\nYour goal is to explore this codebase as grounding for planning and implementation. Say \"Exploration done\" when you are done, do not summarize your findings.\n\nHere is the user request:\n\u003c/user_request\u003e\nThere is a rust compilation error when building this project. Fix it. DO NOT READ PREVIOUS COMMIT.\n\u003c/user_request\u003e","type":"text"}],"role":"user"},{"content":[{"text":"I'll explore the codebase to understand the project structure and find the compilation error.","type":"text"},{"id":"toolu_01K27SNufWAu9EamUC7didKH","input":{"pattern":["**/*.rs","Cargo.toml","Cargo.lock"],"reason":"Need to find all Rust source files and Cargo configuration to understand the project structure and identify compilation errors."},"name":"glob_files","type":"tool_use"},{"id":"toolu_01UtoKX3JvoUmFJcLmG8r3PU","input":{"command":"cd /workspace \u0026\u0026 cargo build 2\u003e\u00261 | head -100","reason":"Run cargo build to see the actual compilation errors.","reason_to_use_instead_of_read_file_tool":"N/A","reason_to_use_instead_of_edit_file_tool":"N/A","reason_to_use_instead_of_glob_files_tool":"N/A"},"name":"bash","type":"tool_use"}],"role":"assistant"},{"content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01K27SNufWAu9EamUC7didKH","is_error":false,"content":[{"text":"/workspace/codex-rs/ansi-escape/src/lib.rs\n/workspace/codex-rs/app-server-client/src/lib.rs\n/workspace/codex-rs/app-server-client/src/remote.rs\n/workspace/codex-rs/app-server-protocol/src/bin/export.rs\n/workspace/codex-rs/app-server-protocol/src/bin/write_schema_fixtures.rs\n/workspace/codex-rs/app-server-protocol/src/experimental_api.rs\n/workspace/codex-rs/app-server-protocol/src/export.rs\n/workspace/codex-rs/app-server-protocol/src/jsonrpc_lite.rs\n/workspace/codex-rs/app-server-protocol/src/lib.rs\n/workspace/codex-rs/app-server-protocol/src/protocol/common.rs\n/workspace/codex-rs/app-server-protocol/src/protocol/mappers.rs\n/workspace/codex-rs/app-server-protocol/src/protocol/mod.rs\n/workspace/codex-rs/app-server-protocol/src/protocol/serde_helpers.rs\n/workspace/codex-rs/app-server-protocol/src/protocol/thread_history.rs\n/workspace/codex-rs/app-server-protocol/src/protocol/v1.rs\n/workspace/codex-rs/app-server-protocol/src/protocol/v2.rs\n/workspace/codex-rs/app-server-protocol/src/schema_fixtures.rs\n/workspace/codex-rs/app-server-protocol/tests/schema_fixtures.rs\n/workspace/codex-rs/app-server-test-client/src/lib.rs\n/workspace/codex-rs/app-server-test-client/src/main.rs\n/workspace/codex-rs/app-server/src/app_server_tracing.rs\n/workspace/codex-rs/app-server/src/bespoke_event_handling.rs\n/workspace/codex-rs/app-server/src/bin/notify_capture.rs\n/workspace/codex-rs/app-server/src/bin/test_notify_capture.rs\n/workspace/codex-rs/app-server/src/codex_message_processor.rs\n/workspace/codex-rs/app-server/src/codex_message_processor/apps_list_helpers.rs\n/workspace/codex-rs